Z||000000||2birds||01-03-2001||11:42 PM||||This came up in the oil filter discussion, and it reminded me of something.<P>The filter my T-bird Super Coupe used had the exact same O-ring diameter and length as a PF 52, but the threads were different.  It used an oil-to-water cooler from the factory, like the 5.0 Mustang Police cars and Lightning Pickups used.  It seems to me that if a correctly threaded adapter was found, this would be a slick setup to use, since the filter pad is so close to the heater hoses anyway.  The actual heat exchanger pad is only about 2 inches thick, so clearance shouldn't be a problem, and a PF 47 is just a shorter version of the 52 if it was.  No air cooler required, no long, leaky, oil hoses to route, and it supposedly helps the car warmup faster.<P>Thoughts?||||reg||1
